<resources>
    <!--
        Oswald Bold, digits and a colon only. The filter is what keeps a bitmap
        font affordable: eleven glyphs instead of a full character set, so the
        atlas is 12 kB rather than hundreds.

        Generated by tools/fontgen. See tools/fontgen/README.md to reproduce.
        Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 — see OFL.txt alongside.
    -->
    <font id="TimeNumbers" filename="time_numbers.fnt" filter="0123456789:"/>

    <!--
        The bottom gauge's readout, at its own smaller size. FONT_XTINY is the
        smallest system font there is — FONT_GLANCE is bigger, not smaller — and the
        gauge wants to sit quieter than a slot value, so it gets its own face.
    -->
    <font id="ArcValue" filename="arc_value.fnt" filter="0123456789%"/>

    <!--
        Slot labels. FONT_XTINY sets a slot's name at nearly the size of its own
        value, in a face wide enough that a real name like "Respiration Rate" was
        never going to fit, so the labels get a condensed uppercase face of their
        own — smaller than the value, tracked out a pixel so all caps still reads
        at a glance.

        Uppercase only, which is what keeps the atlas affordable: 41 glyphs rather
        than the 70-odd a mixed-case set needs. Everything drawn through it is
        uppercased first — see SlotDrawable.
    -->
    <font id="SlotLabel" filename="slot_label.fnt"
          filter="ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789/ -+."/>
</resources>
